verdict:
1.0.3 on 4215 (dennykorsukewitz/Sublime-QuoteWithMarker, ALIVE: last commit 2026-10-07): installs and loads, command quote_with_marker (text) with the palette entry 'QuoteWithMarker: Quote with Marker.' plus keymap and menu. It reads TM_COMMENT_START/TM_COMMENT_END from the view's shellVariables and wraps the selection in a '---' box carrying the marker (default 'MyMarker - ${year}.${month}.${day}', expanded by hand). Works: in a .c file, selecting two lines produced '// ---
// MyMarker - 2026.11.05
// ---
// int a = 1;
// return a;
 int a = 1;
 return a;

// ---' - quoted copy in the C comment style, original selection left in place, date-expanded marker correct; a .py file quoted with '#' the same way. Gap, recorded only (no data loss, arguably by design): on a syntax with no TM_COMMENT_START (Plain text has shellVariables []) the quote characters are empty, so the command emits '---
MyMarker - 2026.11.05
---
' plus the text twice with no comment prefix and no warning - nothing tells the user the file cannot be quoted. No traceback (meta_info returns [], not None). The author already has an open issue about the no-selection path (#1), so nothing new was filed. Removed with remove_packages.

2013.09.14.21.08.13 on 4215 (Andr3as; homepage andrano.de/SurroundWith, source github.com/Andr3as/Sublime-SurroundWith which is ARCHIVED). A SurroundWithCommand taking an action argument (for, if, ifelse, while, dowhile, try, div) with seven ctrl+alt+... bindings, inserting a template around the selection with tab stops. WORKS FOR C-LIKE LANGUAGES BUT NOT FOR PYTHON ON ST4, measured: in a .js view "if" wrapped two lines in "if (/*Condition*/) {
	var x = 1;
	console.log(x);

}" as intended, but in a .py view the same command produced "if (/*Condition*/) {
	x = 1
	print(x)

}" - C braces in Python, which is not valid Python. The cause is in the code: the Python branches compare self.language against the string "Packages/Python/Python.tmLanguage", and ST4 reports Packages/Python/Python.sublime-syntax, so the Python-specific templates are unreachable. The same guard is used for every action (for/while/if/...), so all of them produce braces in Python. Nothing filed: the repository is archived (last push 2013). Checks: install console delta 5 lines, 0 errors, no dialogs; removal 1 line; scratch views closed, temp files deleted.
